  "title": "Monotone mass ratio, upper semicontinuous density and density at least one for minimizing cycles in ℝ^P",
  "statement": "Let P, n ∈ ℕ and let C ∈ 𝒟_n(ℝ^P) (C : GeometricCurrentOn univ n, ℝ^P = Euclid P) be minimizing in ℝ^P (IsMinimizingIn C univ: C is integer multiplicity and M_W(C) ≤ M_W(S) for all admissible competitors) with ∂C = 0 (BoundaryVanishes C). Then: (ii) for every y ∈ ℝ^P the function ρ ↦ ρ^{−n}·M_{B_ρ(y)}(C), written ENNReal.ofReal(1/ρ^n)·C.massOn(ball y ρ) ∈ [0, ∞], is nondecreasing on (0, ∞); (iii) there is an upper semicontinuous Θ : ℝ^P → ℝ with HasMassDensity C y (Θ(y)) for every y ∈ ℝ^P, i.e. Θ(y) ≥ 0 and M_{B_ρ(y)}(C)/(ω_n·ofReal(ρ^n)) → ofReal(Θ(y)) in [0, ∞] as ρ ↓ 0, where ω_n = unitBallVolume n; and (iv) θ ≥ 1 whenever y ∈ spt C and HasMassDensity C y θ.",
  "lean_statement": "∀ (P n : ℕ) (C : GeometricCurrentOn (univ : Set (Euclid P)) n), IsMinimizingIn C univ → BoundaryVanishes C → (∀ y : Euclid P, MonotoneOn (fun ρ : ℝ => ENNReal.ofReal (1 / ρ ^ n) * C.massOn (ball y ρ)) (Ioi 0)) ∧ (∃ Θ : Euclid P → ℝ, (∀ y : Euclid P, HasMassDensity C y (Θ y)) ∧ UpperSemicontinuous Θ) ∧ ∀ y ∈ C.support, ∀ θ : ℝ, HasMassDensity C y θ → 1 ≤ θ",
